  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. Multiplicity sectors in discriminant form\nWith $e_1=\\lambda_1+\\lambda_2$ and $e_2=\\lambda_1\\lambda_2$ (fitted above), set $\\delta_c=\\lambda_c-e_1/2$, so that $\\delta_c=\\pm\\sqrt{D}$ with $D=e_1^2/4-e_2$. Every copy quantity $a_c=A+B\\lambda_c$ then reads $a_c=P(t)+Q(t)\\,\\delta_c$, with $P=A+Be_1/2$ and $Q=B$. The table also lists the contaminated states' $\\hat k$ ratios $\\hat k_{(2,2)}/\\hat k_{(1,1)}$, which test whether $v=6d_{(1,1)}-d_{(2,2)}$ is clean.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "discForm = Table[Module[{rows = Select[fits2, #[[1]] == μ &], e1, e2},\n    {e1, e2} = rows[[1, 4]];\n    {μ, Factor[e1^2/4 - e2], Table[{r[[3]], Factor[Together[r[[4, 1]] + r[[4, 2]] e1/2]], Factor[r[[4, 2]]]}, {r, Rest[rows]}]}], {μ, mult2}];\n(* k(2,2)/k(1,1) for every contaminated state, mult-1 directly and mult-2 via P, Q *)\nratio22 = Join[Table[With[{k = Association[Table[f[[3]] -> f[[4]], {f, Select[fits1, #[[1]] == μc[[1]] &]}]]}, {μc[[1]], Factor[k[\"k{2, 2}\"]/k[\"k{1, 1}\"]]}], {μc, Select[singles, ! cleanQ[#] &]}],\n   Table[With[{pq = Association[Table[x[[1]] -> x[[2 ;; 3]], {x, df[[3]]}]]}, If[KeyExistsQ[pq, \"k{1, 1}\"], {df[[1]], {Factor[pq[\"k{2, 2}\"][[1]]/pq[\"k{1, 1}\"][[1]]], Factor[pq[\"k{2, 2}\"][[2]]/pq[\"k{1, 1}\"][[2]]]}}, {df[[1]], \"clean\"}]], {df, discForm}]];\nColumn[{Grid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"D = δ_c^2\", \"quantity\", \"P(t)\", \"Q(t)\"}}, Flatten[Table[Table[Join[{df[[1]], df[[2]]}, x], {x, df[[3]]}], {df, discForm}], 1]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Join[{{\"contaminated state\", \"k(2,2)/k(1,1)  (mult 2: {P ratio, Q ratio})\"}}, ratio22], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
